## Phase 6 — Validation Checklist

Before declaring the task complete, verify every item:

**System protection**
- [ ] No new design tokens were introduced.
- [ ] No new shared components were created.
- [ ] No existing page, route, or module was modified.
- [ ] Sidebar, topbar, and global layout (`src/shell/`) are unchanged.
- [ ] `src/theme/` files are unchanged.
- [ ] `src/ui/antd.ts` barrel is unchanged (or user approved an addition).
- [ ] No backend files, API routes, server handlers, or database schemas were touched or created.
- [ ] No `fetch`, `axios`, `useQuery`, `useSWR`, or equivalent data-fetching calls were introduced.

**Dummy data**
- [ ] Every table and list in the module is populated with static mock data from `src/<module>/data/`.
- [ ] Each mock data file exports a typed array constant with a matching TypeScript interface.
- [ ] Mock data covers all states and variants visible in the module's flow.
- [ ] Mock data contains realistic values (not placeholder text like "foo" or "test123").
- [ ] No mock data files were placed outside `src/<module>/data/`.

**Token and component hygiene**
- [ ] Every ZIP token has been replaced with a target repo token.
- [ ] Every ZIP component has been replaced with a target repo component.
- [ ] No raw hex, rgba, or arbitrary px values remain in ported files.
- [ ] All antd imports in ported files come from `src/ui/antd.ts`, not from `antd` directly.
- [ ] No ZIP component or token file was added to the target repo.

**UX fidelity**
- [ ] The module's UX flow is identical to the ZIP original.
- [ ] The module's page layouts are visually equivalent to the ZIP original.
- [ ] All relevant UI states are handled: default, loading, empty, error, success, disabled.

**Visual polish (Phase 5h — verify in browser)**
- [ ] No overlapping text, icons, or toolbars (especially narrow sider + main content split).
- [ ] Side-panel list actions stay **inside** the panel — no antd `List.Item` `actions` overflow.
- [ ] No duplicate titles (shell project name, card title, inner section header, wizard sidebar vs content).
- [ ] Typography uses **`hydraTypography`** roles + `hydraTextStyleToReactCss()` — no ZIP font literals.
- [ ] Spacing, borders, radii, shadows from **`theme.useToken()`** / `shellLayout`; search uses **`AppSearchInput`** where applicable.
- [ ] Sider/content split: `overflow: hidden`, content `minWidth: 0`, fixed sider width explicit.
- [ ] Selected / hover list rows match ZIP *behaviour* (chevron default, actions on hover, primary left accent).
- [ ] Alignment checked: toolbars, form columns, table headers, wizard footer actions.

**No duplicate UI on screen (Phase 2f + 5h-B — verify in browser)**
- [ ] Phase **2f** audit done: each ZIP screen marked port / merge / skip before implementation.
- [ ] No construction project picker, project list, or duplicate project **name/title** in module outlet.
- [ ] No second breadcrumb bar, back-to-projects link, or global chrome re-created in module.
- [ ] One section title per region (not Card title + inner panel heading for the same thing).
- [ ] Wizard: step title/description only in content panel; sidebar is compact steps only.
- [ ] One primary CTA per context — not header + empty-state duplicate when list is populated.
- [ ] One loading/error feedback pattern per state (not `Spin` + redundant `Alert` for the same wait).
- [ ] No duplicate status/progress strips for the same background job (match single-strip BOM pattern when applicable).

**Routing**
- [ ] New routes are registered in `App.tsx` but existing routes are untouched.
- [ ] Module routes file follows the `BomRoutes.tsx` pattern.
- [ ] No existing route was reordered or renamed.
- [ ] **Hydra prototype:** no construction project-list or project-picker in the module; pages use
  `useActiveProject()` like `BomLandingPage`, mock data filtered by `projectId`, UI state resets on
  `projectId` change; top bar untouched.

**Naming and structure**
- [ ] Module directory follows the `src/<module>/` convention with correct subdirectories.
- [ ] Page files are under `src/<module>/pages/`.
- [ ] Layout wrapper (if any) is under `src/<module>/layout/`.
- [ ] Module state files (if any) are named `<module>*State.ts` or `<module>*FlowState.ts`.

If any item fails, fix it before finishing. If a fix requires a judgment call, ask the user.

